+directives:
+  directives:
+  - id: TROUPE-001
+    title: Preserve user files byte-for-byte
+    description: >-
+      Never reformat, reorder or rewrite anything in a user's configuration file that the user did not
+      ask to change. Comments, key order, quoting, indentation, blank lines and line endings outside the
+      requested change are preserved exactly. Use round-trip, format-preserving YAML handling; never
+      load-and-dump the whole file. Tests for any file-writing behaviour assert the untouched bytes are
+      identical.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [specify, plan, implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-002
+    title: Conservative choice under uncertainty, stated
+    description: >-
+      When unsure, take the conservative choice that cannot lose or corrupt a user's data (refuse rather
+      than guess; write atomically via temp file + rename in the same directory), and state what was
+      chosen and why. If both troupe.yml and troupe.yaml exist, or input is otherwise ambiguous, stop
+      with an error rather than pick one silently.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [specify, plan, implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-003
+    title: Error messages name the path or file
+    description: >-
+      Every user-facing error message names the configuration path (key path within the YAML) and/or the
+      file involved. Tests assert the path/file appears in the real CLI output.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-004
+    title: Fixed technical constraints
+    description: >-
+      Python 3.12+, managed with uv; the CLI runs as `uv run troupe config ...` from the repository root.
+      The `eventsourcing` library is used for the event store and projection - do not hand-roll a
+      substitute. Configuration lives at `<theatre>/.troupe/troupe.yml` (or `.yaml`). macOS and Linux
+      only; Windows is out of scope. No performance targets - do not trade clarity for speed.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [specify, plan, implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-005
+    title: Tests that prove something
+    description: >-
+      Every behaviour has a test that fails when the behaviour breaks. The test name states what it
+      proves and its body checks exactly that. A test that passes whatever the code does is worse than
+      no test - fix or delete it. Test against real shapes: real files in temporary theatres, real CLI
+      invocations and output, the real eventsourcing library - not hand-written stand-ins.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [plan, implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-006
+    title: Done means verified
+    description: >-
+      Before claiming work is done: run `uv run pytest`, `uv run mypy --strict` and `uv run ruff check`
+      (plus `ruff format --check`) and show the actual output. Never report success from reasoning
+      alone; report failing or skipped checks as such.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-007
+    title: One decision, one named place
+    description: >-
+      Keep each decision (file names and lookup rules, formats, defaults, message wording, event shapes)
+      in one named place - a named constant, function or module - so changing it later is a one-place
+      change rather than a hunt. Build for the current stage only, in a way that is easy to change.
+    severity: warn
+    applies_to: [plan, implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-008
+    title: Whole scope, no invented requirements
+    description: >-
+      Deliver the whole of what is asked; never quietly narrow scope - if something cannot be done, say
+      so. Do not invent requirements: the product owner decides what to build. Before asking, search the
+      repository, the contract and the provided documents; then ask with what was found, the options and
+      a recommendation. Where the contract leaves a choice open, make it and record what was chosen and
+      why.
+    severity: error
+    applies_to: [specify, plan, implement, review]
+  - id: TROUPE-009
+    title: Spec, code and tests move together; decisions recorded
+    description: >-
+      When behaviour changes, update the specification, the code and the tests in the same change.
+      Record significant decisions with their reasons where the next person will find them (decision
+      records in the repository, referenced from the spec/plan). Commit in small, meaningful steps with
+      messages that say why.
+    severity: warn
+    applies_to: [specify, plan, implement, review]
