+    kind: tactic
+    title: Change Apply Smallest Viable Diff
+    summary: Introduce changes using the smallest possible modification that achieves the stated goal, minimising unintended side effects.
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-change-apply-smallest-viable-diff.md
+  - id: TACTIC:clean-linear-commit-history
+    kind: tactic
+    title: clean-linear-commit-history
+    summary: Definition unavailable in bundled doctrine.
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-clean-linear-commit-history.md
+  - id: TACTIC:code-documentation-analysis
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Code and Documentation Analysis for Boundary Discovery
+    summary: "Extract terminology from a codebase and its documentation to identify semantic clusters that reveal implicit context boundaries. Used during domain modelling and architectural review to surface unacknowledged bounded contexts before they calcify into accidental coupling. Success criteria: 100-500 terms extracted, clustered by semantic similarity, clusters mapped to team/directory ownership, proposed boundaries validated with domain experts, and cross-boundary risks identified and documented.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-code-documentation-analysis.md
+  - id: TACTIC:code-review-incremental
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Incremental Code Review
+    summary: Review a change set to identify correctness, structural, and architectural risks without rewriting or expanding scope. Formulate feedback as observations and questions, not instructions.
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-code-review-incremental.md
+  - id: TACTIC:compositional-stream-boundaries
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Compositional Stream Boundaries
+    summary: "Define where reactive streams (RxJS, observables, signals) begin and end within the atomic hierarchy. Prevents stream leak across component boundaries and ensures subscription ownership is explicit.\n"
