+  - id: TACTIC:function-over-form-testing
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Function Over Form Testing
+    summary: "Prioritize behavioral validation over structural verification in test suites. Tests should prove that the system does what it is supposed to do, not that it was assembled from the right parts. Construction details (constructors, builders, accessors) get tested indirectly through functional tests that exercise the objects they create. Core principle: when behavior is tested thoroughly, construction coverage follows naturally.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-function-over-form-testing.md
