+    kind: tactic
+    title: Generated Code Stewardship
+    summary: "Treat generated code as maintainable project code. Agents may improve it, but they must not leave behind bloated, unexplained, untyped, or hard-to-review output simply because it was generated.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-generated-code-stewardship.md
+  - id: TACTIC:glossary-curation-interview
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Glossary Curation Interview
+    summary: Systematically expand a living glossary through structured HiC-led curation rounds, ensuring all new terms are clear, well-grouped, and approved before inclusion.
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-glossary-curation-interview.md
+  - id: TACTIC:input-validation-fail-fast
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Input Validation with Fail-Fast Feedback
+    summary: Validate input data comprehensively before processing to avoid wasting resources on invalid data. Provide clear, actionable feedback on errors while protecting system internals from exposure.
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-input-validation-fail-fast.md
+  - id: TACTIC:interface-variation-design
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Interface Variation Design
+    summary: "Explore materially different interface shapes before committing to a deepened module design. The tactic reduces first-idea bias by comparing interfaces on leverage, locality, misuse resistance, dependency strategy, and how naturally behavior can be tested through the same surface callers use.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-interface-variation-design.md
+  - id: TACTIC:language-driven-design
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Language-Driven Design
+    summary: "Treat language drift as an architectural signal. When terminology becomes inconsistent or ambiguous across code, docs, and conversation, it predicts deeper structural problems. Reviewers use linguistic checks to catch architectural issues before they manifest as bugs or coupling.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-language-driven-design.md
+  - id: TACTIC:locality-of-change
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Locality of Change Assessment
+    summary: "Systematic decision protocol for evaluating whether a proposed change adds necessary complexity or introduces premature abstraction. Implements Directive 024 by giving implementers and reviewers a structured method for assessing scope before committing to a solution. Core principle: do not add complexity to solve problems that do not demonstrably exist. Decision checklist — proceed only if 5+ of 7 apply: (1) Can I point to 3+ real instances where the current approach failed? (2) Have I quantified the impact? (3) Have I evaluated \"do nothing\" as an option? (4) Have I explored simpler alternatives first? (5) Does the change preserve or enhance core architectural values? (6) Am I not prescribing too early? (7) Does the change achieve significant value at proportional cost?\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-locality-of-change.md
