+  - id: TACTIC:secure-design-checklist
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Secure Design Checklist
+    summary: "Apply the nine foundational secure design principles (Saltzer & Schroeder) at the design phase of a new feature or component so that security properties are built in rather than retrofitted. Apply before implementation begins, not after. Principles: (1) Least Privilege — minimum access for minimum time. (2) Fail-Safe Defaults — deny by default, permit explicitly. (3) Economy of Mechanism — keep security paths simple and centralized. (4) Complete Mediation — check every access every time, no indefinite caching. (5) Open Design — security must hold even if the attacker knows the source code. (6) Separation of Privilege — no single condition sufficient to grant access. (7) Least Common Mechanism — do not share access mechanisms unnecessarily. (8) Psychological Acceptability — security must not significantly impede usability. (9) Defense in Depth — layer independent barriers; assume each layer can fail.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-secure-design-checklist.md
+  - id: TACTIC:secure-regex-catastrophic-backtracking
+    kind: tactic
+    title: Secure Regex — Avoid Catastrophic Backtracking
+    summary: "Secure coding practice for designing and reviewing regular expressions so they cannot be driven into pathological matching times by adversarial input (Regular-expression Denial of Service / ReDoS). Backtracking engines may run in exponential or polynomial time when a vulnerable pattern is paired with an input that forces repeated re-matching. This tactic codifies the patterns to avoid, the rewrites that make them linear, and the escape hatches when a linear rewrite is not possible.\nPattern is vulnerable only when the problematic sub-pattern is followed by something that can fail. End-of-input counts as \"something that can fail\" for any full-match (e.g. ``re.fullmatch``). Partial-match APIs (``re.search``, ``re.split``, ``re.findall``) widen the attack surface because the engine retries from the next index on every failure.\n"
+    source_path: ''
+    local_path: _LIBRARY/tactic-secure-regex-catastrophic-backtracking.md
